            "text": "{\"primary_meaning\":\"Eternal life, spiritual flourishing, and the Cross of Christ, often linking the Tree of Life in Eden to the cross of Calvary and the New Jerusalem.\",\"primary_basis\":[\"Genesis 2:9\",\"1 Peter 2:24\",\"Acts 5:30\",\"Revelation 22:2\"],\"alternatives\":[{\"meaning\":\"Individual believers or human beings, whose spiritual state is represented by their health, location near water, and fruitfulness.\",\"basis\":[\"Psalm 1:3\",\"Jeremiah 17:7-8\",\"Matthew 7:17-19\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"Earthly kingdoms, empires, or rulers, whose power and shelter are depicted as a massive, overarching tree.\",\"basis\":[\"Daniel 4:10-12\",\"Ezekiel 31:3-9\",\"Matthew 13:31-32\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"Divine wisdom, which brings life and flourishing to those who embrace it.\",\"basis\":[\"Proverbs 3:18\",\"Proverbs 11:30\"],\"prominence\":\"minority\"}],\"has_settled_consensus\":true,\"confidence\":\"high\",\"notes\":\"The tree is a foundational biblical symbol. It creates a structural bookend in Scripture from the Tree of Life in Genesis to the Tree of Life in Revelation, with the cross of Christ frequently identified as the redemptive tree bridging the two.\"}",
